    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), who enjoys the premier matchup on the board against a vulnerable right-handed starter. With an elite park factor (+16%) and a favorable SP xERA of 4.52, **Gunnar Henderson** is poised for a massive outing; his top-of-the-order positioning (+10%) and dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) make him an absolute must-start. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.41) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.75) round out our tier-one threats, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** specifically benefiting from a high-upside matchup against a pitcher with a 5.14 xERA, while **Kyle Tucker** thrives despite the assumed #6 slot due to superior underlying SP skill projections. We are also monitoring **Jackson Merrill** (73.87) closely; although he faces a tough assignment, his aggressive stolen base potential remains a high-value asset in our 5x5 format, even with the slight penalty for facing an elite defensive catcher.\n\nOn the margins, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (68.57) and **Andy Pages** (68.65) represent our most efficient mid-tier plays. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is a standout selection today, bolstered by a significant dynamic platoon edge (+14%) against a pitcher whose xERA of 4.12 provides a clean runway for production. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Brady House**, who nearly cracked the lineup with a 54.99 score. Ultimately, **Brady House** was relegated to the bench in favor of higher-floor options like **Coby Mayo** (55.64), who\u2014despite being buried in the #8 spot\u2014benefits from the same favorable park factors that elevate the rest of the **Austin Waves** core. \n\nRisks remain, particularly regarding our outfield deployment where **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** are both subject to \"Lineup Pending\" status; should their actual batting orders shift downward, their efficiency scores will require re-evaluation. Additionally, **Drake Baldwin** (53.26) and **Liam Hicks** (43.41) face a stiff test against a left-handed arm, though their integration into the top third of the order provides just enough buffer to keep them in the starting rotation for today's slate. We remain vigilant on wind conditions for **Sam Antonacci** (59.46), whose +5% wind-out adjustment keeps him firmly in the mix despite his relatively modest base projection.",
